<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="SRFR-062" project="set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Add Push Updates ribbon button to Matter AND Project (per SRFR-001 Q-07 finding) via /ribbon-edit</title>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-effort>3h</estimated-effort>
    <actual-effort></actual-effort>
    <assigned>AI Agent</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-group></parallel-group>
    <tags>ribbon,dataverse,field-mapping,wave-6</tags>
    <depends-on>SRFR-061</depends-on>
    <wave>6</wave>
  </metadata>

  <prompt><![CDATA[
Add a "Push Updates to Related Records" ribbon button to BOTH the Matter main
form AND the Project main form. SRFR-001 Q-07 confirmed 2 active profiles
2026-07-02: `Matter to Event` (source: `sprk_matter`) and `Project to Event`
(source: `sprk_project`). Both source entities require the ribbon button.

The ribbon customization mirrors the CANONICAL pattern already shipped for the
Communication Send button at
`infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/CommunicationRibbons/Entities/sprk_communication/RibbonDiff.xml`.
Structure: `<CustomAction>` with unique per-entity ID, `<CommandDefinition>`
with `<EnableRule>` referencing a `<CustomRule Library="$webresource:sprk_fieldmapping_push"
FunctionName="Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile" Default="false">`, and
`<Actions>` invoking `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates` with `PrimaryControl`.

Deploy via the `/ribbon-edit` skill — the round-trip export/edit/import path.
DO NOT hand-edit a solution zip. This is FR-B3-01's deploy path.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>Dataverse ribbon customization author familiar with `RibbonDiffXml`, `CustomAction` / `CommandDefinition` / `EnableRule` / `<CrmParameter Value="PrimaryControl" />` patterns, and the `/ribbon-edit` skill's round-trip workflow.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
Ribbon `CustomAction` "Push Updates to Related Records" is deployed to the
Matter main form (and any additional parent forms from Q-07 inventory) on
spaarkedev1. The button is enabled only when
`Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile(primaryControl)` returns true; on
click, it invokes `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates(primaryControl)`. The
RibbonDiffXml is versioned in the repo under
`infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/MatterRibbons/` (or the equivalent path per
existing convention). Import completes cleanly and UAT verifies visibility +
invocation.
  ]]></goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-claude">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="canonical-pattern">infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/CommunicationRibbons/Entities/sprk_communication/RibbonDiff.xml</file>
    <file purpose="wave-0-inventory">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/notes/wave-0-discovery.md</file>
    <file purpose="skill">.claude/skills/ribbon-edit/SKILL.md</file>
    <file purpose="webresource-dependency">src/client/webresources/js/sprk_fieldmapping_push.js</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-B3-01">Ribbon button is scoped to parent forms whose entity appears as `sourceEntity` in at least one active `sprk_fieldmappingprofile`. Matter is the guaranteed minimum. Additional forms per SRFR-001 Q-07 inventory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="repo pattern">Ribbon structure MUST mirror the Communication Send button pattern at `infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/CommunicationRibbons/Entities/sprk_communication/RibbonDiff.xml`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="repo pattern">`CustomAction` IDs are unique per entity (e.g., `sprk.matter.fieldmapping.push.CustomAction`). Reuse of an ID across entities is an import failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="repo pattern">Deploy via `/ribbon-edit` skill (export solution → unpack → edit RibbonDiff.xml → repack → import). Do NOT hand-edit a solution zip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="dependency">Web resource `sprk_fieldmapping_push` must be deployed to the target environment before the ribbon customization imports successfully (`$webresource:sprk_fieldmapping_push` reference).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">EnableRule's `Default` attribute is `false` — the button is hidden unless `hasSourceProfile` explicitly returns true.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>dataverse/ribbon-customization</topic>
    <files>
      <file>infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/CommunicationRibbons/Entities/sprk_communication/RibbonDiff.xml</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ribbon-edit/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="CustomRule EnableRule against webresource function" location="Communication Send button RibbonDiff.xml"><![CDATA[
        `<EnableRule Id="...">
           <CustomRule Library="$webresource:sprk_fieldmapping_push"
                       FunctionName="Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile"
                       Default="false">
             <CrmParameter Value="PrimaryControl" />
           </CustomRule>
         </EnableRule>`
      ]]></pattern>
      <pattern name="Actions block invoking webresource function" location="Communication Send button RibbonDiff.xml"><![CDATA[
        `<Actions>
           <JavaScriptFunction Library="$webresource:sprk_fieldmapping_push"
                               FunctionName="Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates">
             <CrmParameter Value="PrimaryControl" />
           </JavaScriptFunction>
         </Actions>`
      ]]></pattern>
      <pattern name="LocLabels for accessibility" location="Communication Send button RibbonDiff.xml"><![CDATA[
        Every user-facing string (Button label, tooltip title, tooltip description, alt-text) is a `<LocLabel>` with a `LanguageCode="1033"` entry — do NOT inline literals.
      ]]></pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      Ribbon-based invocation is the correct surface for a single-command action
      that operates on the current record (per ADR-006 UI Surface Architecture).
      This surface has one canonical pattern in the repo — the Communication
      Send button — and mirroring it minimizes ribbon-customization drift. The
      `/ribbon-edit` skill handles the export/edit/import round-trip so we
      don't hand-modify solution zips (a known source of import failures).
    </background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="SRFR-061" status="pending">
        `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js` webresource must be authored and its
        `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile` + `pushUpdates` functions
        must exist. The ribbon references them by name.
      </dependency>
      <dependency task="SRFR-001" status="assumed-complete">
        Wave 0 discovery Q-07 identified the full set of parent forms that need
        the button. Matter is guaranteed; others per that inventory.
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>SRFR-082 (Wave 8) deploys web resources + ribbon customizations to UAT.</item>
      <item>Communication Send button is the closest canonical pattern.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context Check">Verify context &lt; 60%. Read SRFR-061 acceptance criteria to confirm the webresource is ready. Read the Communication Send button RibbonDiff.xml as the pattern reference.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Q-07 Inventory Load">Read `notes/wave-0-discovery.md` for the Q-07 parent-form inventory. Matter is guaranteed; enumerate any additional entities requiring the button (list may be empty for MVP).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author Matter RibbonDiff">Author (or amend) `infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml` with a `CustomAction` under `Mscrm.Form.sprk_matter.MainTab.Actions.Controls._children` (or the correct group per canonical pattern). Fields: unique ID `sprk.matter.fieldmapping.push.CustomAction`, sequence value picked to avoid collision.</step>
    <step order="3" name="CommandDefinition + EnableRule">Add `&lt;CommandDefinition Id="sprk.matter.fieldmapping.push.Command"&gt;` with `&lt;EnableRule&gt;` referencing `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile` (Default="false") and `&lt;Actions&gt;` invoking `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates`. Pass `&lt;CrmParameter Value="PrimaryControl" /&gt;` to both.</step>
    <step order="4" name="LocLabels">Add `&lt;LocLabels&gt;` for label ("Push Updates"), tooltip title, tooltip description, alt-text. LanguageCode 1033 minimum.</step>
    <step order="5" name="ModernImage">Reference a ModernImage icon (e.g., "Sync" or "Send") consistent with the canonical Communication pattern.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Repeat for Q-07 Entities">For each additional parent entity in Q-07 inventory, repeat steps 2-5 with a per-entity unique CustomAction ID (e.g., `sprk.&lt;entity&gt;.fieldmapping.push.CustomAction`). If the inventory is Matter-only, skip.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Deploy via /ribbon-edit">Invoke the `/ribbon-edit` skill to execute the round-trip: `pac solution export` → unpack → apply edited RibbonDiff.xml → repack → `pac solution import` targeting spaarkedev1. Capture the import log.</step>
    <step order="8" name="UAT Smoke">In spaarkedev1: open a Matter record. Confirm the "Push Updates" button appears ONLY when at least one active `sprk_fieldmappingprofile` has sourceEntity=sprk_matter. Click the button; confirm dialog appears; on confirm, `pushUpdates` runs; toast reports outcomes.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Update Task Status">Update TASK-INDEX.md 🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-062. Reset current-task.md for next task.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="Read">Read canonical RibbonDiff.xml, Wave 0 inventory, skill definition</tool>
    <tool name="Write">Create MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml</tool>
    <tool name="Edit">Amend existing RibbonDiff.xml if one already exists for Matter</tool>
    <tool name="Bash">Run `pac solution export/import` orchestrated by /ribbon-edit</tool>
    <tool name="Skill:/ribbon-edit">Round-trip export/edit/import path</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="artifact">infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml (created or amended)</output>
    <output type="artifact">Ribbon customizations for any additional Q-07 entities (path per repo convention)</output>
    <output type="notes" ephemeral="true">Solution import log excerpt in notes/mda-form-notes.md or new notes/wave-6-ribbon-deploy.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-062)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">RibbonDiff.xml exists in the repo for Matter (and any additional Q-07 entities) with a `CustomAction` referencing `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`EnableRule` references `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.hasSourceProfile` with `Default="false"`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CustomAction IDs are unique per entity (grep confirms no duplicates across the repo).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deploy via `/ribbon-edit` completes with zero import errors on spaarkedev1.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAT: ribbon button appears on Matter form when at least one active `sprk_fieldmappingprofile` has sourceEntity=sprk_matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAT: ribbon button hidden when no matching profile exists (or on a Matter that has none associated as source).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UAT: click → confirm dialog → confirm → toast reports push outcomes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
